# .agent/settings.local — machine-local settings (issue #386)
#
# Copy this file to .agent/settings.local (git-ignored) in the main
# checkout and fill in the paths. Nothing here is published; the repo
# never names a path on your machine.
#
# One `key=value` per line. Lines starting with `#` are ignored. The file
# is read, never sourced. A value starting with `~/` is under your home
# directory; a relative value is taken relative to this file's directory
# (.agent/), so prefer an absolute or `~/` path for files outside the repo.
# Scripts run from a workspace worktree fall back to the main checkout's
# copy of this file.
#
# inbox       one file, for this machine, that capture.sh appends one-line
#             thoughts to. The directory must already exist.
# run_record  one file the sit-rep appends a dated line to on each run, so
#             the next run can say what moved.
#
#inbox=~/<notes-dir>/inbox.txt
#run_record=~/<notes-dir>/sitrep-runs.txt
